course: dictionary
lesson: 237
title: Allow: let it happen
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Allow usually means to let someone do something, or to give permission. «Dogs are not allowed in the café.» Nobody has given dogs permission to come in.
explain: Allow can also mean to make something possible. «The bridge allows people to cross the river.» The bridge does not give anyone permission. It makes crossing possible.
explain: Allow can mean to plan or keep time, money or space for something. «Allow ten minutes to walk to school.» It means keep ten minutes free for the walk, so you do not rush.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a word like let or make possible, and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Allow» is a verb, so it changes: allow, allows, allowed, allowing.
fact: «Allow» means to let someone do something, or to give permission.
fact: «Allow» can also mean to make something possible, as in «The bridge allows people to cross.»
fact: «Allow» can mean to plan or keep time, money or space for something.
fact: Useful phrases: be allowed to, allow for, and not allowed. «Phones are not allowed in class» means the rule says no phones.
exercise: «Dogs are not allowed in the café.» What does not allowed mean here? | * Permission is not given | Very hungry | Very happy | Very fast
exercise: «The bridge allows people to cross the river.» What does allows mean here? | Shouts across the water | * Makes it possible | Stops the river forever | Paints the river
exercise: «Allow ten minutes to walk to school.» What should you do with the ten minutes? | * Keep them free for the walk | Spend them on sweets | Give them to a friend | Forget the walk
test: Which sentence shows that permission is given? | The door is red. | The rain is falling. | * You are allowed to borrow a book.
test: In «The umpire will not allow it», what does allow mean? | Plays it in a game | Gives it a prize | * Does not give permission for it | Paints it blue
exam: Which phrase from this lesson means against the rules? | * not allowed | be allowed to | allow for
